      "writtenOn": "2023-08-24T14:09:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should check if headset supports LC3 codec. If yes, LC3 codec should be enabled regardless of headset supporting Aptx voice codec. \n\nIf headset supports only Aptx voice codec, we need to select Aptx voice codec.",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a903c93_35f2e03a",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1974186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T12:16:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While I was trying to implement this check if peer supports LC3 I started wondering if such checks: \n```\n(p_scb-\u003epeer_codecs \u0026 BTM_SCO_CODEC_LC3)\n```\n\nwon\u0027t collide with:\n```\n(p_scb-\u003epeer_codecs \u0026 BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q0_MASK)\n```\nand they will. How can we go around that?",
      "parentUuid": "008c16ce_55a652b9",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df33ac89_35f8662e",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1974186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-28T09:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok I think I could use p_scb-\u003eis_swb_codec to ensure it\u0027s aptx. Do you agree?",
      "parentUuid": "5a903c93_35f2e03a",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53102265_82a82978",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1974186
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-28T13:12:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Finally, I am not using is_swb_codec...\nPlease check the current version.\nWhile we save peer codecs, we set LC3 codec status and later it is taken into consideration while enabling aptx: if LC3 SWB is supported on headset you are not allowed to change aptx_swb_codec_status and it\u0027s status remains as \u0027false\u0027, which should disable aptx swb even if supported. Please let me know if it is correct and acceptable.",
      "parentUuid": "df33ac89_35f8662e",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "762ff7b1_f13e9429",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1902235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-28T17:56:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jakub, could you please change BTM_SCO_CODEC_LC3 macro definition to avoid this? LC3 over HFP is not yet commercialized, so we don\u0027t break functionality by changing its definition.",
      "parentUuid": "df33ac89_35f8662e",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79f7d9a4_d39fb784",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T01:34:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at the code, I\u0027m not sure to understand why we should change `BTM_SCO_CODEC_LC3` and not `BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q0_MASK` as neither of those value are serialized or send over the air.\n\nI agree that we should modify one of the two because they are conflicting, but I think we should modify `BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q0_MASK` and all the other Q1, Q2, Q3 and move it alongside `BTM_SCO_CODEC_LC3` (in btm_api_types.h).\n\nWhile looking at the code I also found strange that we set `BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q1_MASK`, `BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q2_MASK`, `BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q3_MASK` but never test for those bits.",
      "parentUuid": "762ff7b1_f13e9429",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c579ff62_75977eed",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/hfp/HeadsetService.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 1199,
      "author": {
        "id": 1902235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-31T14:50:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree that. I was suggesting to change BTM_SCO_CODEC_LC3 only instead of changing definitions of BTA_AG_SCO_SWB_SETTINGS_Q0_MASK, and Q1, Q2, Q3 as it needs more changes relatively.\n\nQ1, Q2 and Q3 settings are not supported as of now. They will be supported in future hence they are not yet checked anywhere. They can be place holders for now.",
      "parentUuid": "79f7d9a4_d39fb784",
      "revId": "889e78a0cade1616102c8c77f8f4cf097d4d886a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
